<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Chakiris v&rsquo;Kablanus<br>[Laws of Leasing and Contracting]</div>

<div class="halacha-title">[Continuation of Halacha 5]</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;45</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">chakiris v&rsquo;kablanus</span> [leasing and contracting] &mdash; that the loss is attributed to the lessee and contractor more than to the owner of the house, as is explained in the Shulchan Aruch and is brought above.</p>

<p>For the essential rectification of the labor of the field, that it should succeed in its work, is drawn from the true sages who engage in the Torah in truth and exert themselves in it, until they innovate in the Torah true chiddushim that bring about good deeds, and compose holy books through which the Torah is completed, as above. And from them is drawn the rectification of the labor of the field.</p>

<p>For the holy Torah is called a field, and a vineyard, and a garden, and an orchard &mdash; as is brought in many verses and in the words of our Sages of blessed memory. For each person must exert himself in the Torah until he produces fruits &mdash; so that he should not be, G&ndash;d forbid, a dry tree, but rather should be in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;A fruit tree producing fruit according to its kind&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 1:11)</span> &mdash; as is brought. That is, that he should innovate in the Torah and derive from the Torah true counsels for himself and for his fellows, and judgments of upright practices, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And from these true sages is drawn the power and the life-force for all who work in the field, that they should succeed in their labor. And therefore their entire rectification is through emunas chachamim &mdash; from which is all their life-force, as above. For the corruption of the field, G&ndash;d forbid, is drawn from the sin of Adam HaRishon, from the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Cursed is the ground on your account,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 3:17)</span> &mdash; may the Merciful One save us &mdash; because he blemished emunas chachamim, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the entire rectification is through emunas chachamim. For the sages who toil in the Torah, as above, are in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He who works his land will be satisfied with bread&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Mishlai 12:11)</span> &mdash; the bread of the Torah [lachma d&rsquo;Oraisa]. For they toil to produce fruits and to succeed in their labor. For regarding them it is said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And he shall be like a tree planted by streams of water, that gives its fruit in its season,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 1:3)</span>. Therefore through them is the entire rectification of the field and the vineyard, etc., as above.</p>

<p>And therefore when there is, G&ndash;d forbid, a loss and a corruption of the field &mdash; that it was blighted, etc. &mdash; which is drawn from the blemish of emunas chachamim, as above &mdash; therefore for the most part the damage is attributed to the lessee and contractor. For he has already fallen into the aspect of servitude, since he hired himself out to work in the fields of others &mdash; which is drawn from the blemish of emunas chachamim, as is explained above in &sect;28 in the Laws of Hiring Workers. Therefore the damage to the field, which is drawn from this blemish, as above, is attributed to him more.</p>

<p>For the essential rectification of the field, that it should produce fruits and succeed properly, is through the true sages, as above. And one must believe in them. For through the complete emunah in the sages, the books of the Torah are multiplied, as above &mdash; and it is considered as if he himself innovated them and composed them. And through this his field will produce fruits and will succeed, as above. Amain v&rsquo;amain.</p>

